      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242047",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/26/2623c8d677c487c1a440ae90325bfc22c9af18eaca680b430be1314c0fdf4da6.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $AK^(\u2015)$, $BL^(\u2015)$, and $CM^(\u2015)$ are the medians of $\u25b3ABC$ and $G$ is its centroid. Select the correct options in the derivation of the coordinates of $G$ below.\n\nSince $AK^(\u2015)$ is a {{field-1}}, we have that $K$ is the {{field-2}} of $BC^(\u2015)$. So, if $(x_{K}, y_{K})$ are the coordinates of $K$, by the\n{{field-3}},\nwe have\n$\\frac{x_{B} + x_{C}}{2}$ {{field-4}} {{field-5}}"
