      ":question/problem": "![](images/c6/c666158598adbcc89fd294b3ec76a0d4ba5fd9447eb4f62469d28a6a23fb936a.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $PK^(\u2015)$, $QL^(\u2015)$, and $RJ^(\u2015)$ are the medians of $\u25b3PQR$ and $G$ is its centroid. Select the correct options in the derivation of the coordinates of $G$ below.\n\nSince $PK^(\u2015)$ is a {{field-1}}, we have that $K$ is the {{field-2}} of $QR^(\u2015)$. So, if $(x_{K}, y_{K})$ are the coordinates of $K$, by the\n{{field-3}},\nwe have\n$\\frac{x_{P} + x_{R}}{2}$ {{field-4}} {{field-5}}"
